{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: forecasts are systematically below realized prices across most of the 30-day horizon (often by ~2–8 EUR), especially during strong uptrends.",
    "Trend underreaction / lag: when the recent history is accelerating upward, the forecast path increases too slowly and peaks too early; apply a trend-following uplift to days ~1–20.",
    "Excess mean-reversion at long horizons: forecasts drift back toward ~73–77 even when outcomes stay elevated (~80–84); reduce mean-reversion strength beyond ~day 10–15.",
    "Late-horizon downside overshoot: in several cases the model turns bearish too much near days ~25–30 (drops into high-60s/low-70s) while outcomes remain mid/high-70s; cap late-horizon drawdowns unless recent history shows a clear reversal.",
    "Level anchoring to recent average: forecasts appear anchored to the last-30-day mean rather than the new regime; add a regime-shift adjustment when the last 5–10 days break above the prior 30-day range."
  ]
}
